comment:
Soft-float internals: __make_fp builds a newlib _fp_float structure from four words and
packs it via __pack_f. Compiler helper for constructing floats in software (no FPU on W806);
return value is passed back through the ABI float register.

Arm UART interrupt-driven receive: only when the UART is READY and RX is not busy;
stores the buffer/size, sets RxState to BUSY_RX (0x22), enables the RXNE and error interrupt
sources (INTS |= 0x1ec) and unmasks them (INTM &= ~0x1ec). Returns HAL_BUSY otherwise.

Initialize a PWM channel from hpwm->Init: calls HAL_PWM_MspInit, then configures output
mode, counter mode, frequency (prescaler/period), duty, auto-reload preload and output inverse;
finally clears the break/dead-time bit (CR bit 12 for channel 0, CH4CR3 bit 2 for channel 4).

Converts a raw 7-segment mask from the DMM display (bit0=a .. bit6=g) to ASCII:
06->'1', 5B->'2', 4F->'3', 66->'4', 6D->'5', 7D->'6', 07->'7', 7F->'8', 6F->'9';
special codes 31/50->'r', 38->'L', 39->'C', 79->'E'; 00->0xFF (blank), unknown->0.

DMM subsystem update, called from the main loop:
- if the modes-menu flag is set, draws the DMM modes menu at the current selection;
- when the DMM is enabled, no menu is open and settings[1] != 5, parses a received packet when the
  RX buffer starts with 'Z',0xA5 (zw_dmm_parse_rx_packet);
- when the DMM window is not already shown and no menu is open, opens it (zw_dmm_window).

Firmware UART upgrade entry point (alt boot/upgrade menu).
Prints 'start download...', stops the watchdog, resets the UART RX fifo, then:
1) zw_uart_upgrade_prepare_hw_setup(baudrate) - fails => 'uart download init failed', 1 s delay, return 0;
2) zw_fpga_init_upgrade_sequence_logic() - fails => 'uart init flash failed', 1 s delay, return 0;
3) zw_fpga_firmware_upload(firmware_version_select_) - fails => 'uart update logic failed', 1 s delay, return 0;
On success prints 'upgrade successful' and re-arms the watchdog. Returns the last status (non-zero ok).

printf output helper: writes a reversed character buffer (least-significant digit first)
to the output sink, inserting leading and trailing spaces per width and left-align flags;
returns the updated output index.
